<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:22:53Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>EU summit: European leaders pledge support for Ukraine's Zelenskyy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:52498e1ae42616b1f3bf6168937775742deb9e6c8a0bae0c84f177e1e8f865e6</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:22:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T13:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-summit-european-leaders-pledge-support-for-ukraine-s-zelenskyy/a-79678808--2db8721d89a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-summit-european-leaders-pledge-support-for-ukraine-s-zelenskyy/a-79678808?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Zelenskyy has received words of encouragement from EU leaders who pledged support for Ukraine's self-defense against Russia. This comes as winter approaches and the US seems to be withdrawing support.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The EU wants an AI revolution. But on whose terms?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ab36f5f3b345bd8d299797fce4baff89c3b218e5bd3c48de7d00558c69e134a</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:22:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T13:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-eu-wants-an-ai-revolution-but-on-whose-terms/a-79673456--ab198d15d72f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-eu-wants-an-ai-revolution-but-on-whose-terms/a-79673456?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the US and China race ahead, the European Union seeks to boost its economy with AI. Can it compete while protecting workers, safety and the climate?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany, France agree on deal to support Europe's struggling car industry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57decffb753f58dde4e20026b9c2ed976d923b61d5a0e9999de388a61a2c63c0</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:22:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-france-agree-on-deal-to-support-europe-s-struggling-car-industry/a-79678595--5e23597ac466.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-france-agree-on-deal-to-support-europe-s-struggling-car-industry/a-79678595?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The two countries said the agreement aimed to safeguard Europe's automotive industry, encouraging development and research. Automakers in Europe have so far struggled to compete with Chinese electric car companies.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India's young workers have a new colleague: AI</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54edfe9292b8958f08e295bf9dd5d91d48a18ea00d7f193119996d6580101ea1</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:22:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T11:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-young-workers-have-a-new-colleague-ai/a-79678342--60612fda0623.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-young-workers-have-a-new-colleague-ai/a-79678342?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Artificial intelligence is changing the way Indian workplaces operate — raising questions about productivity, skills and entry-level jobs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>German lawmakers back monthly state pension contributions for children, with families able to add more</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d10672efa2e52bc5d9fb6cef0126f3540bd9dd0e9cb718aece8eaf691f60b0c</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:22:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T11:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-lawmakers-back-monthly-state-pension-contributions-for-children-with-families-able-to-add-mor/live-79678671--02713419dab3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-lawmakers-back-monthly-state-pension-contributions-for-children-with-families-able-to-add-more/live-79678671?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's parliament has backed a plan to help children save for retirement from the age of six. Meanwhile, Jewish students report death threats after they confronted a far-right lawmaker. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How prepared is Kenya for an Ebola outbreak?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2a186c8dca7cd6037bbaf423d88ac0003bdb57ef2e35cede02006f19fc7a65a</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:22:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T10:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-prepared-is-kenya-for-an-ebola-outbreak/a-79668144--2b6e19c28555.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-prepared-is-kenya-for-an-ebola-outbreak/a-79668144?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The first two confirmed Ebola cases in Kenya have raised urgent questions about the country's public health preparedness and border controls. But the health ministry says there is no need for panic.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Italy cuts air traffic in half amid data transmission issue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:178e2288dd58f0811484d94c29cc620ec19a0d469659f658142fbb8d529c5387</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:22:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T10:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/italy-cuts-air-traffic-in-half-amid-data-transmission-issue/a-79678133--8d0677d89358.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/italy-cuts-air-traffic-in-half-amid-data-transmission-issue/a-79678133?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Citing problems with the data transmission network, Italian authorities have drastically reduced the volume of flights in their airspace. The ENAV authority ruled out malicious activity and said flights remained safe.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Clashes erupt at Argentine student protests against President Milei's austerity policies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:82bda858bc1b1598ee11b6599684f7579d96e5ec22c5341ef6fb3751d7361cb5</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:22:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/clashes-erupt-at-argentine-student-protests-against-president-milei-s-austerity-policies/a-79676861--35bb07407c1a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/clashes-erupt-at-argentine-student-protests-against-president-milei-s-austerity-policies/a-79676861?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Demonstrators clashed with police as President Javier Milei's decision not to release funding for universities brought students and employees to the streets. Protesters say the country's future is at stake.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Who was Eva Mamlok? Berlin square renamed after Jewish anti-fascist resistance fighter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d893f36a3a35e474b1000f1a6ebd7908cce23af7245fd63f3c12882b11978d1</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:22:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-was-eva-mamlok-berlin-square-renamed-after-jewish-anti-fascist-resistance-fighter/a-79668919--fa371a8e7f27.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-was-eva-mamlok-berlin-square-renamed-after-jewish-anti-fascist-resistance-fighter/a-79668919?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She started taking action against Hitler as a teenager and never stopped until her death in a concentration camp. Berlin's Blücherplatz is now being renamed after her.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Europe promotes sovereign, trusted AI as it struggles to catch US and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6299c4dd197c0e3ecfdbbe66c726b2263d6cd86193f25a130887127aed13fdbf</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:22:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/europe-promotes-sovereign-trusted-ai-as-it-struggles-to-catch-us-and-china/a-79667770--a2cc0238c9e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/europe-promotes-sovereign-trusted-ai-as-it-struggles-to-catch-us-and-china/a-79667770?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At an international AI summit in Dublin, European leaders promoted trusted and independent AI. Critics question whether the EU can close the gap with the US and China while maintaining strict regulation.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Formula One in Rwanda: Sportswashing claims vs. hopes for African legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a964b6e713757dbd8efd3f6db52a83ee08170de9e6bfa49730663d33aceeb78</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:22:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T08:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/formula-one-in-rwanda-sportswashing-claims-vs-hopes-for-african-legacy/a-79650744--59b33a158fd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/formula-one-in-rwanda-sportswashing-claims-vs-hopes-for-african-legacy/a-79650744?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Formula One will return to Africa for the first time since 1993. There is concern Rwanda are using it as another sportswashing opportunity, but there is also hope the event's legacy can impact wider African society.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>California wildfires force evacuations near Malibu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:494c02cc8f6a1ff9698c174525e498b590c0a57d09ae5bc889e4a3ea0e5df5a7</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:22:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T08:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/california-wildfires-force-evacuations-near-malibu/a-79676355--23636ff902db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/california-wildfires-force-evacuations-near-malibu/a-79676355?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A fast-moving fire near Malibu has forced evacuations. Stronger overnight winds threaten to spread the flames further.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wildfire kills 4 firefighters in Indonesia's Mount Bromo national park</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15b0fcb9a2b81b94121c254c20d481eb23f5f589015fc20d31cbcfe039fc5094</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:22:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T08:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wildfire-kills-4-firefighters-in-indonesia-s-mount-bromo-national-park/a-79676291--7fc8c1dafd75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wildfire-kills-4-firefighters-in-indonesia-s-mount-bromo-national-park/a-79676291?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The latest victims of Indonesia's wildfires were trapped by thick smoke and fast-spreading flames, authorities said. Meanwhile, the toxic haze from the fires has spread to Indonesia's neighbors.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India: CJP's Dipke detained amid call for fresh Delhi demo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64eb602f3fded89551786150766493605303e36a7216eea5c45a824fed0d1e61</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:22:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T06:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-cjp-s-dipke-detained-amid-call-for-fresh-delhi-demo/live-79675849--c55ce4c4fba8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-cjp-s-dipke-detained-amid-call-for-fresh-delhi-demo/live-79675849?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police placed the founder of the Cockroach Janta Party, Abhijeet Dipke, in preventive detention. He was calling for a protest in central Delhi in defiance of a court order banning it. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Starlink: How Elon Musk's company influences geopolitics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58e7cb7c2ba0e912ee2f90ec6bf445a8676e98d9457ea1603790ad163bf7125f</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T05:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/starlink-how-elon-musk-s-company-influences-geopolitics/a-75963477--2578f6b76007.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/starlink-how-elon-musk-s-company-influences-geopolitics/a-75963477?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Designed to bring internet access to remote regions, Elon Musk's Starlink has become vital in crisis regions and war zones. But Ukraine also shows the risks of depending on the service.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Carney implies US trying to 'break' Canada amid vote for Alberta independence referendum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a6062355f93f13cff8b74ff1facc110f6dc93d2343be2cbfc7c24fe261fb0a63</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:22:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T04:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/carney-implies-us-trying-to-break-canada-amid-vote-for-alberta-independence-referendum/a-79675652--c6d8b1a483f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/carney-implies-us-trying-to-break-canada-amid-vote-for-alberta-independence-referendum/a-79675652?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The oil-rich province of Alberta will vote to decide if it wants to remain a Canadian province or start the legal process toward separation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Oregon school shooting: Gunman kills 3 students and teacher before being shot dead by community member</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b24269323b54b92c41c65fb05b8bbb597549a374a4a9ec6851ee97256e8d7a6</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:22:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T21:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oregon-school-shooting-gunman-kills-3-students-and-teacher-before-being-shot-dead-by-community-membe/a-79674849--fb10caf1772b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oregon-school-shooting-gunman-kills-3-students-and-teacher-before-being-shot-dead-by-community-member/a-79674849?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A 16-year-old gunman opened fire at an elementary school in Bend, Oregon, killing three children and a teacher. Two others were wounded. A community member pursued and killed the suspected shooter, authorities said.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bus, train collide, injuring 19 at Channel Tunnel terminal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:284109a1397f99aec1a1235d6e34beed72b49d6dcd64097a9cbef1c758e994bb</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T20:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bus-train-collide-injuring-19-at-channel-tunnel-terminal/a-79674671--04ade7f3eab7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bus-train-collide-injuring-19-at-channel-tunnel-terminal/a-79674671?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A minibus carrying truck drivers collided with a freight train near the Channel Tunnel entrance in France, injuring 19 people, two of them severely. Authorities launched an inquiry into what caused the accident.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Venezuela's Nicolas Maduro pleads not guilty to torture charges</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ae324e0cccef7f5d9f3e38fa53902b04bf6f16c66003ed76c14b4910a519ea0</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T18:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/venezuela-s-nicolas-maduro-pleads-not-guilty-to-torture-charges/a-79673496--661837b93a79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/venezuela-s-nicolas-maduro-pleads-not-guilty-to-torture-charges/a-79673496?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Maduro and his wife were charged with leading a state-sponsored repression campaign that tortured scores of victims during his presidency from 2013 to 2026.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Self-replicating AI: Is your fridge a cybersecurity risk?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f11bedc805d9c7d2258f932a004005e62933e8ca38b5eeb1e699c9bd59c3130b</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T18:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/self-replicating-ai-is-your-fridge-a-cybersecurity-risk/a-79662958--8f5eea61704f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/self-replicating-ai-is-your-fridge-a-cybersecurity-risk/a-79662958?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Anthropic researchers warn that AI worms could soon target connected household devices and spread from one device to another. Cyberattacks on French supermarkets illustrate just how vulnerable such systems can be.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East updates: Houthis target Yemen government palace in Aden</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ced91f9c265852dd43b4bf6519bd4c1c8cc648d434dfc3cc9449ad3f63a8baa</id><updated>2026-10-16T13:21:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T17:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/middle-east-updates-houthis-target-yemen-government-palace-in-aden/live-79672880--01517cb5752d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/middle-east-updates-houthis-target-yemen-government-palace-in-aden/live-79672880?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Houthi rebels say they targeted Saudi military assets in a rare attack on the interim seat of Yemen's internationally recognized government. Meanwhile, vessels are again under fire near the Strait of Hormuz. More on DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
